^{:go/end 277} (go/method deriveReturnFlagsFromCallee "deriveReturnFlagsFromCallee tries to set properties for a given\nreturn result where we're returning call expression; return value\nis a return property value and a boolean indicating whether the\nprop is valid. Examples:\n\n\tfunc foo() int { return bar() }\n\tfunc bar() int { return 42 }\n\tfunc blix() int { return 43 }\n\tfunc two(y int) int {\n\t  if y < 0 { return bar() } else { return blix() }\n\t}\n\nSince \"foo\" always returns the result of a call to \"bar\", we can\nset foo's return property to that of bar. In the case of \"two\", however,\neven though each return path returns a constant, we don't know\nwhether the constants are identical, hence we need to be conservative.\n" [^{:tag (* resultsAnalyzer)} ra ^ir/Node n] :results [ResultPropBits bool]
  (when (!= (.Op n) ir/OCALLFUNC)
    (return 0 false))

  (let [ce (assert (* ir/CallExpr) n)]
    (when (!= (.Op (.-Fun ce)) ir/ONAME)
      (return 0 false))

    (let [called (ir/StaticValue (.-Fun ce))]
      (when (!= (.Op called) ir/ONAME)
        (return 0 false))

      (let [cname ^{:go/via [nameFinder]} (.funcName ra called)]
        (when (== cname nil)
          (return 0 false))

        (let [calleeProps (propsForFunc (.-Func cname))]
          (when (== calleeProps nil)
            (return 0 false))

          (when (!= (len (.-ResultFlags calleeProps)) 1)
            (return 0 false))

          (return (aget (.-ResultFlags calleeProps) 0) true))))))
